{
  "key": "iiot-retrofit",
  "name": "Brownfield Plant IIoT Retrofit",
  "category": "OT",
  "description": "A brownfield process plant whose serial field equipment reaches the network through gateways. PLANT-SERIAL: a Moxa NPort 5650-16 in the MCC room (port 1: four ABB ACS580 drives polled as Modbus RTU over raw TCP 4001; port 3: two SEL-351S relays polled over DNP3 serial on TCP 4003), an MGate MB3170 Modbus TCP -> RTU gateway in front of six PowerLogic PM5330 meters, and an NPort 5150 whose boiler RTU (an end-of-life SCADAPack 334E) a Windows 7 HMI reaches through a RealCOM virtual COM port (TCP 950 + 966); a transient engineering laptop runs the Moxa device search (UDP 4800 broadcast). IIOT-FIELD: Kerlink and MultiTech LoRaWAN gateways forward Milesight / Dragino sensor uplinks to the network server in the DMZ over the Semtech UDP packet forwarder (1700/udp). BMS-SC: Desigo PXC5 controllers and a JACE-8000 hold BACnet/SC WebSocket connections over TLS 1.3 to a Contemporary Controls BASrouterSC hub (opaque on the wire). The 21 devices behind the gateways are listed in tgt inventory with 'behind' set: known assets that a passive monitor cannot discover as IP assets. Run: tgt run --env iiot-retrofit --pcap iiot.pcap --once --rate 0",
